'''Gerdis''' was a [[Gender|male]]<ref name="OYL AD" /> [[human]] who was apart of the [[Maya Pei Brigade]] during the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="OYL" /> In [[4 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> Gerdis, along with several other members of the brigade, were stranded on the [[moon]] [[Yavin 4]]. Once the human [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] arrived on the moon in a [[TIE Avenger prototype|TIE Avenger]] for a [[Theft of the TIE Avenger prototype|mission]] related to the [[Axis network]], tensions in the brigade arose. After a [[blaster]] shootout,<ref name="OYL" /> Gerdis and<ref name="Sagrona Teema">{{Andor|Sagrona Teema}}</ref> his<ref name="OYL AD" /> rival [[Bardi]] attempted to negotiate who would depart playing a game of [[Five Hands]] with [[Roski rules]]. During their match, the two heard a loud rumbling that sounded like thunder. A moment later, a [[Yavinian doodar]] barged in and engulfed the two in its mouth, [[Death|devouring]] them.<ref name="Sagrona Teema" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Gerdis first appeared in the [[One Year Later|first]]<ref name="OYL" /> and [[Sagrona Teema|second]]<ref name="Sagrona Teema" /> episodes of the [[Andor Season 2|second season]] of the television series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', created by Tony Gilroy.<ref name="OYL" /> He was portrayed by [[Sam Gilroy]], who is the son of series creator [[Tony Gilroy]].<ref name="Trivia">{{SW|url=news/andor-trivia-guide-week-3|text=Secrets from the Set of ''Andor'' Season 2: Week 3 Trivia}}</ref>

